{
  "title": "Humeral Shaft Fracture - Pediatric",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4005/humeral-shaft-fracture--pediatric",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Mar 7 2024",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Humeral Shaft Fractures in the pediatric population are usually traumatic in nature, although nonaccidental trauma and pathologic lesions can not be overlooked.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with plain radiographs.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is almost always immobilization due to the high remodeling potential of the pediatric humerus.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "represent **<10% of humerus fractures** in children",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**mechanism of injury**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**typically associated with trauma**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathomechanics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**neonates**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "hyper-extension or rotational injury during birth",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "**adolescents**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually direct trauma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathophysiology",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "consider a **pathologic** process if fracture is a result of a low energy mechanism",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "may be associated with **child abuse** if age <3 and fracture pattern is spiral",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**radial nerve palsy**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "associated with up to 5% of humeral shaft fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history of traumatic event",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "arm deformity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "inspection",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "mid-arm swelling and deformity",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "open fractures are rare",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "palpation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tenderness to palpation",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "motion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "weakness or absence of wrist and digit extension if radial nerve palsy is present",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "pseudoparalysis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "irritability or refusal to move upper limb in neonates",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "reflexes remain intact",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "3",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "recommended views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**full length AP and lateral views of humerus**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4005/images/screen%20shot%202012-07-27%20at%208.34.27%20am.jpg",
                      "caption": "XRAY of left humerus shaft fx"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "optional views",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**orthogonal views of shoulder and elbow**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "required to rule out associated injuries",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "findings",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "typical fracture patterns are transverse and oblique",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "examine closely for pathologic lesions",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "immobilization in splint or brace",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "utilized for almost all pediatric humeral shaft fractures (if not pathologic) due to remodeling potential",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "acceptable alignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "younger children",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "< 35-45 deg angulation",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "older children",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": [
                            {
                              "text": "< 20 deg varus/valgus",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "< 20 deg procurvatum",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "<15 deg rotation malalignment",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            },
                            {
                              "text": "< 2cm shortening",
                              "table": null,
                              "images": [],
                              "importance": "2",
                              "children": []
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sling and swathe or cuff and collar in young children",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Coaptation splint or hanging arm cast",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "Sarmiento functional brace in older children/adolescents",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ROM exercises can be initiated in 2-3 weeks once pain is controlled",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "open reduction internal fixation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "open fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "multiply injured patient",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ipsilateral forearm fractures",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "\"floating elbow\"",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "associated shoulder injury",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "unacceptable alignment",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "techniques",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "flexible intramedullary nail fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [
                        {
                          "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4005/images/screen%20shot%202012-07-27%20at%2011.56.50%20am.jpg",
                          "caption": "XRAY of L humerus fx after fixation"
                        }
                      ],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "anterior, anterolateral or posterior approach with 3.5mm or 4.5mm plate fixation",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Radial nerve palsy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs in <5%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "most commonly associated with middle and distal 1/3 fractures",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "typically due to a neuropraxia",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "spontaneous resolution is expected",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "exploration is rarely needed",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "if function has not returned in 3-4 months, EMGs are performed and exploration considered",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Malunion**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rarely produces functional deficits, due to the wide range of motion at the shoulder",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "up to 20-30° of angulation is associated with excellent outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Delayed union**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "may consider ultrasound bone stimulation",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Limb length discrepancy**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "commonly occurs, but rarely causes functional deficits",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Physeal growth arrest**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "proximal and distal humerus growth plates contributes 80:20 percent to overall humeral length",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Excellent",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "associated with enormous remodeling potential and **rarely requires surgical intervention**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/4005/images/figure-3_remodelling_humeral-shaft.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "up to 20° of angulation is associated with excellent outcomes due to the large range of motion of the shoulder",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
